  "context": "## Optimization, Coherence, and the Frame\nWhy a system optimizing on its own map cannot see the map; why coherence — not rationality — is the mode that sees it; and why a purely maximizing agent is structurally blind to exactly the capabilities that keep a system alive.\n\nDocument Status — Working Paper 2 · Series: Informational Friction (a systems theory)\n\nBuilds on Paper 1 ( The Map and the Flow ), which established the object: a representation used as a control surface, diverging from the flow it governs, with back-action. This paper supplies the agent-level mechanism beneath that object. The forward forecasts (the Outlook) and the consolidated falsification battery are deferred to later papers in the series; falsifiable claims are marked inline.\nEtiquetas: Casos de uso y aplicaciones 15.39%; Investigación y documentación técnica 30.77%; Experimentación, falsación y contraejemplos 38.46%; Cambio de perspectiva 15.38%\nFicha: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/optimization-coherence-and-the-frame-t1487/\nDocumento de origen: https://tegrity.ai/1487-2/\n\n",
